From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: André Braga <code@andrebraga.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: suspend the card with the system

The card registered no PM ops, so the ASoC core never suspended its
streams and they kept running through system suspend. Use
snd_soc_pm_ops, as the sc7180 and sc7280 cards do.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -644,6 +644,7 @@
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "snd-sc8280xp",
 		.of_match_table = snd_sc8280xp_dt_match,
+		.pm = &snd_soc_pm_ops,
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(snd_sc8280xp_driver);
